o Sanz París is a distinguished medical professional serving as the Head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section at Hospital Universitario Miguel Servet in Zaragoza. He specializes in nutrition and dietetics, with a particular focus on diabetes care. In addition to his role as head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section, Dr. Sanz París also holds the position of technical director and leads the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the same hospital. His expertise and leadership contribute significantly to the management and treatment of nutritional and dietary needs in patients.", "FRANCISCO LOSFABLOS CALLAU:Dr. Francisco Losfablos Callau is a medical professional specializing in nutrition and dietetics, working alongside Dr. Alejandro Sanz París at Hospital Universitario Miguel Servet.", "OLVEIRA ET AL.:Olveira et al. conducted a study in Spain that focused on two main aspects related to hospitalized patients, particularly those with diabetes. The first aspect of their research observed the prevalence of enteral nutrition among these patients, highlighting its significance in their care. Additionally, the study examined the costs associated with diabetes care in hospitalized patients, providing insights into the financial implications of managing diabetes in a hospital setting. Through their comprehensive analysis, Olveira et al. contributed valuable information to the understanding of nutritional and economic factors affecting diabetes care in Spain.", "SANZ PARIS ET AL.:Sanz París et al. conducted a significant study in 2013 on malnutrition prevalence among hospitalized diabetic patients in Spain.", "COSTES DE ATENCIÓN DE LA SALUD:Healthcare costs associated with diabetes in Spain, which were studied to understand the economic impact of the disease.", "HOSPITALES:Hospitals are healthcare institutions dedicated to providing treatment and care for patients, including those who require specialized services such as parenteral nutrition and catheter insertion. They often operate under management contracts to deliver a range of medical services. In addition to medical care, hospitals also serve food products, such as Galleta Maria, and must provide allergen information to ensure patient safety. In Spain, hospitals are involved in research studies focusing on diabetes and malnutrition among patients, highlighting their role in evaluating and addressing nutritional needs through initiatives like Nutrition Day. Overall, hospitals are essential institutions that not only deliver health services but also prioritize the nutritional well-being of their patients.", "GASTO TOTAL DEL SISTEMA NACIONAL DE SALUD:Total expenditure of the National Health System in Spain, which includes costs related to diabetes management.", "ÚLCERAS DE DECÚBITO:Pressure ulcers that are a significant concern for diabetic patients, as highlighted in various studies.", "RIESGO DE AMPUTACIÓN:Risk of amputation associated with diabetes, particularly in patients with diabetic foot complications.", "MEDICARE:Medicare is a U.S. federal health insurance program that provides coverage primarily for individuals aged 65 and older, as well as some younger individuals with disabilities. The program is designed to assist with healthcare costs and has been involved in studies related to various health conditions, including diabetes and malnutrition. Medicare offers essential support for individuals with diabetes and other medical conditions, ensuring access to necessary healthcare services.", "GERIATRIC RESIDENCE:Geriatric residences are facilities that provide care for elderly individuals, often focusing on their specific health needs, including diabetes management and nutritional support."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}